(Objective: Conduct a comprehensive meta-analysis examining the effects of all relevant exercise) Tj
T*
(training modes on resting blood pressure to establish optimal antihypertensive exercise) Tj
T*
(prescription practices.) Tj
T*
(Design: Systematic review and network meta-analysis.) Tj
T*
(Data sources: PubMed \(Medline\), the Cochrane Library, and Web of Science.) Tj
T*
(Results: Analysis of 270 randomised controlled trials \(15,827 participants\) showed significant) Tj
T*
(blood pressure reductions across multiple exercise modes. Isometric exercise training produced) Tj
T*
(the largest reduction at -8.24/-4.00 mm Hg \(systolic/diastolic\), with combined training at) Tj
T*
(-6.04/-2.54 mm Hg. By effectiveness the ranking was: isometric exercise first, then combined) Tj
T*
(training, dynamic resistance training, aerobic training, and high-intensity interval training) Tj
T*
(\(isometric SUCRA 98.3%\). Isometric wall squats were the most effective submode for systolic) Tj
T*
(blood pressure.) Tj
T*
(Conclusions: Various exercise training modes improve resting blood pressure, particularly) Tj
T*
(isometric exercise; the findings are intended to guide future hypertension prevention and) Tj
T*
(treatment guidelines.) Tj
